implementationPlan.description:
TESTS FIRST (DoD 2), plus the CI wiring and a pre-existing break this task's gate depends on. Reference bytes, all verified by an architect dry run, are in /mnt/d/moe-scratch/plan-a7d0/ref/ (outside the repo):
- fix.diff, all 6 files: sha256 e839b6c5c1d8a54217a4063f3252601d45992ca158fbfa28b7168ec3f0fb7939; `git apply --check` OK on 19d5e67a;
- account-wait-attempt.test.mjs: sha256 cdf71c646b510d53d1b882084cca7fe279e729d267aa5d2eab6792e4b744ef2c;
- dryrun.txt: the numbers below.
Copy them with your Edit/Write tools only (project rail); never `git apply` and never cp into the tree. Work in your .worktrees/<taskId> copy.
(a) Create scripts/tests/account-wait-attempt.test.mjs from the reference. It is a node:test slice harness shaped like the launcher half of moe-account-lease.test.mjs (mem:pattern-preflight-block-slice-test-over-postflight-arm). It cuts the REAL code out of each wrapper and runs it against a scripted daemon (the moe_rpc / Invoke-MoeRpc stub is the fake proxy):
- sh: idle_wait, moe_attempt_read + pin_attempt_identity, the lease block, and the launch lines from `    clear_account_lease` + the `if [ "$MOE_SKIP_LAUNCH" != true ] && [ "$CLI_TYPE" = claude ]; then` line to `    CLI_LAUNCHED_AT=$(date +%s)`;
- ps1: Get-MoeProp, the Test-MoeGeneration..Set-MoeAttemptIdentity block, the lease block, and the launch lines from `    Clear-MoeAccountLease` + the `if (-not $moeSkipLaunch -and $cliType -eq 'claude') {` line to the next `    if ($moeSkipLaunch) {`.
Those cuts run in a pass loop modelled on a --no-loop / -NoLoop main loop:
- sh: `while :; ... break; done`;
- ps1: `do { } while ($script:AccountRelaunch)`, which is how the real do/while keeps a -NoLoop run going.
Scenario: pass 1 pins attempt-a (generation 6) on task-wait. With CLOSE_AT, the stub rewrites attempt-a as closed and opens a peer's attempt-b during the wait. Pass 2 pins attempt-c on task-next.
Rows per engine (Linux /bin/bash; win32 powershell.exe, pwsh.exe and Git Bash; an engine that does not start is skipped):
1. a pin closed during the account wait launches nothing and re-runs pre-flight;
2. an untrusted-account wait re-verifies the pin the same way;
3. a pin still current after the wait launches on it;
4. a lease that did not wait keeps the launch path unchanged. The harness starts with the waited flag preset to true, so a missing reset fails here.
(b) scripts/tests/moe-account-lease.test.mjs, +2 lines: in shLeaseScript, after the `sleep()` stub, add a comment and `between(launcherSource('sh'), '# An externally killed idle/backoff sleep must not end the seat under set -e', '# moe_rpc TOOL ARGS_JSON')`. At HEAD its /bin/bash rows 3 and 4 fail with `idle_wait: command not found`: d94c095f made get_account_lease call idle_wait, and the cut never defined it. The gate in step 5 runs that file.
(c) .github/workflows/ci.yml: append ` scripts/tests/account-wait-attempt.test.mjs` to the end of the 'Test agent runtime discovery' run line, after moe-account-lease.test.mjs. That step runs on ubuntu, windows and macOS.
(d) RED evidence, posted as a task comment with moe.add_comment. Run:
`R=/mnt/d/moe-scratch/red-a7d0; rm -rf "$R"; mkdir -p "$R" && git archive 19d5e67a scripts | tar -x -C "$R" && cp scripts/tests/account-wait-attempt.test.mjs "$R/scripts/tests/" && cd "$R" && node --test scripts/tests/account-wait-attempt.test.mjs; "/mnt/c/Program Files/nodejs/node.exe" --test 'scripts\tests\account-wait-attempt.test.mjs'`
The dry run got 2 fail / 2 pass under WSL bash and 6 fail / 6 pass on Windows. Rows 1 and 2 fail on every engine with `LAUNCH task=task-wait attempt=attempt-a generation=6 resume=1` printed right after `[account] MOE_ACCOUNT_LEASED account=acct-1 usage=10%`. Quote those lines in the comment.
Keep every cut anchor above byte-identical in the wrappers (mem:gotcha-wrapper-slice-tests-execute-text). In this test's harness the waited flag is preset to true, so the reset added in steps 2-3 is what rows 3 and 4 depend on.

sh launcher (DoD 1). Edit scripts/moe-agent.sh in place with your TOOL-witnessed editor; it is your worktree copy, and no seat runs it. Reference: /mnt/d/moe-scratch/plan-a7d0/ref/moe-agent.sh.ref (sha256 f8bfda82c5a9adc81eafb0c59e5e0c7681bba1b1999e3c4ba622aeacc14f27c6) and its fix.diff hunks. Insert lines only, +27 in total, and reflow nothing. The CQ-M07 row 91ee455a edits this file at ~7265-7590 (the landing functions), far from these hunks.
(1) get_account_lease (~9085):
- `ACCOUNT_LEASE_WAITED=false` as the first line after its `local` line, before any early return;
- `ACCOUNT_LEASE_WAITED=true` on the line before `idle_wait "$trust_sec"` (the MOE_ACCOUNT_UNTRUSTED branch);
- `ACCOUNT_LEASE_WAITED=true` on the line before `idle_wait "$f1"` (the MOE_ACCOUNT_WAIT branch).
(2) A new function `account_wait_recheck`, with its comment block, between get_account_lease's closing `}` and the `# The guard program runs from a function...` comment (~9157). It does the following, in order:
- return 0 unless `${ACCOUNT_LEASE_WAITED:-false}` = true;
- return 0 unless both MOE_ATTEMPT_ID and MOE_ATTEMPT_GENERATION are set;
- return 0 when `detail=$(moe_attempt_read "$MOE_ATTEMPT_ID" "$MOE_ATTEMPT_GENERATION" 2>&1 >/dev/null)` succeeds. That is the existing store reader, also used by record_candidate_rpc. It fails when the attempt is closed, superseded by another open attempt, missing, or not running/finalizing;
- otherwise print with account_say exactly: `MOE_ACCOUNT_WAIT_STALE_ATTEMPT task=$PREFLIGHT_TASK_ID attempt=$MOE_ATTEMPT_ID generation=$MOE_ATTEMPT_GENERATION (${detail:-attempt not current}) - the claim ended while this seat waited for an account; not launching the pre-wait prompt, re-running pre-flight now.`;
- then `live_marker_remove "$PREFLIGHT_TASK_ID" || true` (it removes only this session's own marker), `clear_account_lease`, give back one resume attempt (`if [ "${RESUME_ATTEMPTS:-0}" -gt 0 ]; then RESUME_ATTEMPTS=$((RESUME_ATTEMPTS - 1)); fi`), set `ACCOUNT_RELAUNCH=true` (the loop top then skips the poll sleep), and `return 1`.
(3) In the launch block (~10741), right after `        get_account_lease` inside its if: `        account_wait_recheck || continue`. Keep `continue` at the call site, never inside the function. The `||` keeps set -e from ending the seat. The pre-flight top (~9589) blanks MOE_ATTEMPT_ID/GENERATION and PREFLIGHT_TASK_ID, so the stale pin cannot leak into the next pass. Under --no-loop, the `continue` skips the end-of-loop break, so pre-flight runs once more.
Error handling: any moe_attempt_read failure (an unreadable store, a python error) counts as not current. The seat then launches nothing and re-runs pre-flight, which is fail-closed, and that pre-flight's own claim and pin decide the launch. The function never exits or deregisters the seat and sends no RPC. A restart needs a NEW wait to fire again, because the flag is reset at every lease, so it cannot busy-loop.
Do not name any variable MOE_ACCOUNT_*: parity-check extracts `\bMOE_ACCOUNT_[A-Z0-9_]*\b` tokens as codes. Use only bash-3.2 syntax (macOS CI runs this file's cuts). Leave the two wait messages' wording unchanged; parity-check pins 'the held task stays held.' in both twins.
Check: `bash -n scripts/moe-agent.sh`; then `node --test scripts/tests/account-wait-attempt.test.mjs` turns its 4 Linux rows green.

Verification (DoD 1-3). Run the checkRef ONCE from the worktree root, exactly as written; copy also in /mnt/d/moe-scratch/plan-a7d0/ref/checkref.txt, sha256 5d33bc72f34fafc4bb6b2899c5bcfad5a65df3a28275abc4d38ded8ea770f2b1. It chains:
- `bash -n scripts/moe-agent.sh`;
- a PS 5.1 ParseFile of scripts/moe-agent.ps1, which prints `ParseFile OK`;
- `bash scripts/tests/parity-check.sh`, with MOE_* scrubbed. It compares the MOE_ACCOUNT_ code family, so MOE_ACCOUNT_WAIT_STALE_ATTEMPT must be in both twins;
- WSL node 24 `--test` of account-wait-attempt + moe-account-lease;
- Windows node.exe `--test` of the same two files. Your worktree is on D:, so Windows can reach it (mem:gotcha-launcher-ps1-rows-from-wsl).
The architect's run on the patched tree exited 0: ParseFile OK; PASS parity-check.sh; WSL `tests 45 pass 44 fail 0 skipped 1`; Windows `tests 67 pass 65 fail 0 skipped 2`. Total about 3 min.
Error handling for a red run:
- `idle_wait: command not found` means step 1(b) is missing.
- A `missing boundaries:` assertion means a wrapper edit moved a cut anchor; restore the anchor.
- A Windows-only failure with no assertion output: re-run that file alone through node.exe and read its first failing row.
- Never weaken a row or a skip to get green.
That run's fresh output is the complete_task evidence. The landing's qualityGate (parity-check + npm run lint) runs again at completion.

Adversarial self-review of this task's diff (load adversarial-self-review). Mutants run in a copy OUTSIDE the worktree: a crash mid-mutant must never leave one in W, where your landing would commit it. Set it up with `git archive HEAD scripts .github/workflows/ci.yml | tar -x -C /mnt/d/moe-scratch/mut-a7d0/<m>`, then `cp --parents` your 6 changed files into it, apply ONE exact-count string edit per mutant, and run that copy's account-wait-attempt.test.mjs. Every mutant must fail at least one row; the dry run confirmed all of these (dryrun.txt):
- M1: drop sh `ACCOUNT_RELAUNCH=true`. Row 1 fails with `PREFLIGHT 2 relaunch=false`.
- M6: drop sh's `[ "${ACCOUNT_LEASE_WAITED:-false}" = true ] || return 0` line. Row 4 fails.
- M7: drop ps1 `$script:AccountRelaunch = $true`. Rows 1 and 2 fail on powershell.exe and pwsh.exe, because the -NoLoop do/while ends without a launch.
Then read the diff for:
- two seats on one task: the re-check only reads .moe/attempts and removes only this session's own marker;
- --no-loop vs -NoLoop: a single extra pass;
- a hot reload (sh exec keeps env, but the pre-flight top re-blanks the pair);
- a daemon restart during the wait: a `reconciling` attempt reads as not current, and the re-run pre-flight's reattach_own_attempts handles it;
- no bash-4-only syntax in the new sh lines (macOS bash 3.2);
- the stale line identical in both twins;
- no new MOE_ACCOUNT_* variable names;
- the wait-message wording untouched.
The diff stays about +279/-2 (net 277), under the 400 review cap. If this review changes any byte, re-run step 5's command and submit that fresh output.

compatibility:
These cut anchors stay byte-identical, because other tests execute them:
- sh: '# printf, not echo -e: a reason from the daemon is printed as is.', "# Runs inside the CLI's subshell", '# An externally killed idle/backoff sleep must not end the seat under set -e', '# moe_rpc TOOL ARGS_JSON', "# Candidate evidence is pinned outside the CLI's mutable context projection.", 'moe_evidence_rpc() {', '    CLI_LAUNCHED_AT=$(date +%s)';
- ps1: "# One line from moe-account-lease.mjs ('' when it printed nothing)", '# The values never leave this process', '# Immutable claim tokens belong to the runner, not the mutable CLI context.', "# A daemon restart parked this seat's attempt in `reconciling`", '    if ($moeSkipLaunch) {'.

